    "category": "class",
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You've built a prosthetic device from the same materials as your pawns. It lets you replace or augment a limb, or add a simple new non-prehensile limb, such as a tail. Crafting a new limb is a 1-hour activity that requires a flat work surface and 1 Bulk of the appropriate materials; attaching it later is a 3-action activity with the manipulate trait.</p><p>Your new limb grants you an unarmed attack based on your Craft: Flesh Craft's poisoned barbs (1d8 poison, brawling, agile, deadly d8, finesse, poison, unarmed); Ethereal Craft's morphic weapon (1d6, brawling, agile, finesse, parry, unarmed, versatile B/P/S); Elemental Craft's elemental launcher (ranged 20 ft, 1d8, sling, modular cold/electricity/fire, scatter 10 ft, unarmed); or Sympathetic Craft's ethereal claw (1d8 spirit, brawling, finesse, spirit, unarmed, with the effects of a ghost touch property rune).</p>"
    },
